  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x{y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+1)^{3}}x{y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{1}^{(x+1)^{3}}{y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [3{y}^{1/3}]_{y=1}^{y=(x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3x(x+1-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
